@user.sigil from User import { user identity, user identifier }

component Profile {
    goal {
        Stores editable *UserProfile* information for a signed-in user identity.

        Keeps UserProfile presentation details separate from authentication identity
        and session rules.
    }

    interface {
        A UserProfile has a user identifier, *display name*, and optional
        *profile-picture URL*.

        Its *public profile summary* contains the same user identifier and
        display name, plus the profile-picture URL when present.

        The owner of a UserProfile can retrieve it by user identifier and request
        its public profile summary.

        The owning user identity can update the display name, the
        profile-picture URL, or both; an omitted field remains unchanged.

        A successful update returns the updated UserProfile.

        Booking and room views can request the public profile summary for display.
    }

    state {
        A UserProfile can be incomplete or complete.

        A UserProfile belongs to exactly one user identifier.

        A profile-picture URL can be absent or present.
    }

    logic {
        A new UserProfile starts incomplete.

        The owning user identity can update the display name and
        profile-picture URL.

        Booking and room views read the public profile summary for display only.

        Authentication does not depend on UserProfile completeness.
    }

    constraints {
        Profile owns the non-authentication fields in UserProfile.

        Auth owns the credentials, sessions, roles, and permission checks associated
        with the user identity.

        Other modules use the public profile summary for display instead of reading
        Auth's private user details.
    }

    cases {
        The owner of a UserProfile updates its display name.

        The owner of a UserProfile sets its profile-picture URL.

        An incomplete UserProfile does not prevent its owner from booking a room.
    }
}
